/T (Dynamic programming \(DP\) is a problem-solving technique that breaks down complex problems into smaller, simpler sub-problems. For each sub-problem, DP computes and stores the solution instead of solving the problem as a whole. When the same subproblem arises, DP uses the already computed solution instead of re-computing it, which significantly reduces computation time. DP is widely used in computer science, mathematics, bioinformatics, and other fields.)
